                    "propertyValues": {
                        "html": {
                            "type": "TRANSLATION_LITERAL",
                            "value": {
                                "code": null,
                                "comment": "",
                                "message": "<p data-end=\"620\" data-start=\"297\">A Hardware Security Key is a small physical device used to verify a user&rsquo;s identity as a second factor in Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). After entering a password, the user interacts with the key typically by plugging it into a USB port or tapping it via NFC on a mobile device. A common example is the YubiKey.</p>\n<h4 data-end=\"644\" data-start=\"622\"><strong>How It Works</strong>:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li data-end=\"644\" data-start=\"622\">The user inserts the security key into a USB port or taps it on a mobile device via NFC.</li>\n<li data-end=\"644\" data-start=\"622\">The system prompts users to touch the key (usually a button or sensor) to confirm their presence.</li>\n<li data-end=\"644\" data-start=\"622\">Authentication is completed without the need to enter a code manually.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4 data-end=\"934\" data-start=\"920\"><strong>Advantages</strong>:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"934\" data-start=\"920\">Provides strong, phishing-resistant authentication.</li>\n<li data-end=\"934\" data-start=\"920\">Operates without requiring mobile devices or network connectivity.</li>\n<li data-end=\"934\" data-start=\"920\">Supports secure use across multiple systems and services.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-end=\"1460\" data-start=\"1243\">On the ServiceNow platform, hardware security keys can be integrated as part of MFA Factor Policies to provide high-assurance authentication.<br data-end=\"1391\" data-start=\"1388\">For more details, please refer to the official <a href=\"/api/now/v1/context_doc_url/mfa-setup-hardware-key-auth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">product documentation</a>.</p>"
                            }
                        }
                    },
